      "edition": "Wednesday 18 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "World Cup build-up",
          "heading": "Fiji to host Samoa, Tonga and Australia A in World Cup warm-up",
          "body": "The inaugural Quad Series, set for July next year, will run in place of the Pacific Nations Cup, Fiji Rugby Union chief executive Koli Sewabu has confirmed. He said Fiji needed more quality matches before the World Cup, with Australian Government funding making it possible. Suva is the preferred venue, though Sewabu said \"it'll all depend too on availability of accommodation.\" Two further matches, involving Japan and then South Africa, are locked in, the second about two weeks before the tournament starts."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Japan lose 15-78 to England in Nations Championship",
          "body": "Argentina beat Italy 19-14 in Nations Championship. Scotland's Scott Cummings out of Japan game with leg damage."
        }
      ]
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-18",
      "edition": "Wednesday 18 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "MND fundraiser",
          "heading": "England to wear Moody's 'Front Up' MND boots against All Blacks",
          "body": "Lewis Moody, the 2003 World Cup winner who captained England at the 2011 tournament, says he has been buoyed by the squad's backing. Players will wear training tops and specially painted boots promoting his 'Front Up' campaign at Saturday's test against New Zealand. Diagnosed with MND last year, Moody is asking supporters to walk one of 175 routes, each 26 miles long, across England, Scotland and Wales on 12 June, his birthday. The aim is to raise more than £1m. \"To have their buy-in is wonderful for me,\" he said."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Japan lose 15-78 to England in Nations Championship",
          "body": "Argentina beat Italy 19-14 in Nations Championship. Scotland's Scott Cummings out of Japan game with leg damage. Fiji confirm Quad Series to replace Pacific Nations Cup."
        }
      ],
