    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-18",
      "edition": "Wednesday 18 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Scrum rematch",
          "heading": "Joe McCarthy says Ireland pack goes into Springboks rematch with 'no fear'",
          "body": "Ireland lock Joe McCarthy, who missed the 24-13 defeat by South Africa in November 2025 through injury, told Virgin Media Sport the forwards have \"definitely gone hard at it\" on the set-piece before Saturday's Nations Championship test in Dublin. In that loss, Springboks head coach Rassie Erasmus' side won penalty after penalty at the scrum, with looseheads Andrew Porter and Paddy McCarthy both yellow-carded. Rather than containing South Africa, the second-row said Ireland will look to attack the game, going in with the mindset that \"every contact matters.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Japan lose 15-78 to England in Nations Championship",
          "body": "Argentina beat Italy 19-14 in Nations Championship. Scotland's Scott Cummings out of Japan game with leg damage. Fiji confirm Quad Series to replace Pacific Nations Cup."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
