      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-18",
      "edition": "Wednesday 18 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Front-row view",
          "heading": "Italy prop Simone Ferrari flags Fiji's physicality before Round 6 test",
          "body": "Benetton front-rower Simone Ferrari, one of six props in Italy head coach Gonzalo Quesada's squad, said Fiji have players with great physicality. The Round 6 meeting is Italy's last match of the Nations Championship pool stage. They come into it off the 14-19 defeat by Argentina in Genoa — a fifth loss in five. Ferrari, who has 75 caps, will learn whether he starts when Quesada announces the team on Thursday, with a team run at the Bluenergy Stadium to follow."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Japan lose 15-78 to England in Nations Championship",
          "body": "Scotland's Scott Cummings out of Japan game with leg damage. Fiji confirm Quad Series to replace Pacific Nations Cup."
