      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Attack plan",
          "heading": "Carter Gordon backs Wallabies to 'flip the switch' on attack against Wales",
          "body": "Wallabies fly-half Carter Gordon said wet Murrayfield conditions dragged the 15-12 defeat to Scotland — his Test return after a broken leg in Argentina — into a territory battle, but he is confident the brand built over the past 12 months can return against Wales. He set up wing Harry Potter's early try, yet assistant coach Tom Donnelly said Australia carried too high into Scotland's choke tackles and must get their body height down. Wales arrive off a drought-breaking win over the All Blacks that broke the tackle record."
        },
        {
